  "'I'm fine,' she said, in the universal tone that meant she was absolutely, categorically, the opposite of fine.",
  "'Let me be perfectly clear,' he began, before saying the most confusing thing I'd ever heard in my life.",
  "'How hard can it be?' she asked — four words that had launched a thousand disasters.",
  "'I've got a bad feeling about this,' he said, 'which I realize I say before literally everything, but this time I mean it.'",
  "'I'm listening,' she said, folding her arms in a way that communicated very clearly that she was not, in fact, listening.",
  "'There's been a slight change of plans,' he announced, 'by which I mean the original plan is on fire, both literally and metaphorically.'",
  "'I don't mean to be dramatic,' she began, before saying the most dramatic thing anyone had ever said.",
  "'I did not see that coming,' he admitted, 'which is embarrassing because that is literally my one job.'",
  "'The difference between genius and stupidity is results,' she explained, 'and unfortunately, we won't know which this is for another twenty minutes.'",
  "'Is this legal?' he asked. 'Probably not,' she replied, 'but I checked with a lawyer and they said it was interesting, which is almost as good.'",
  "'I'm going to do something incredibly stupid,' she announced, 'and I need you to be my witness — not to stop me, just to film it.'",
